{"surah": 84, "verses": [{"ayah": 1, "text": "إِذَا ٱلسَّمَآءُ ٱنشَقَّتْ ", "translation": "When the sky has split [open]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِذَا", "translit": "āَhdِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلسَّمَآءُ", "translit": "ُءٓāَmَّslٱ", "root": "سمو"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱنشَقَّتْ", "translit": "ْtَّqَhsnٱ", "root": "شقق"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 2, "text": "وَأَذِنَتْ لِرَبِّهَا وَحُقَّتْ ", "translation": "And has listened [i.e., responded][1] to its Lord and was obligated [to do so]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَأَذِنَتْ", "translit": "ْtَnِhdَaʾَw", "root": "اذن"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لِرَبِّهَا", "translit": "āَhِّbَrِl", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَحُقَّتْ", "translit": "ْtَّqُḥَw", "root": "حقق"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 3, "text": "وَإِذَا ٱلْأَرْضُ مُدَّتْ ", "translation": "And when the earth has been extended[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَإِذَا", "translit": "āَhdِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلْأَرْضُ", "translit": "ُḍْrَaʾْlٱ", "root": "ارض"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "مُدَّتْ", "translit": "ْtَّdُm", "root": "مدد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 4, "text": "وَأَلْقَتْ مَا فِيهَا وَتَخَلَّتْ ", "translation": "And has cast out that within it[1] and relinquished [it]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَأَلْقَتْ", "translit": "ْtَqْlَaʾَw", "root": "لقي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مَا", "translit": "āَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "فِيهَا", "translit": "āَhyِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "وَتَخَلَّتْ", "translit": "ْtَّlَhkَtَw", "root": "خلو"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 5, "text": "وَأَذِنَتْ لِرَبِّهَا وَحُقَّتْ ", "translation": "And has listened [i.e., responded] to its Lord and was obligated [to do so] –", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَأَذِنَتْ", "translit": "ْtَnِhdَaʾَw", "root": "اذن"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لِرَبِّهَا", "translit": "āَhِّbَrِl", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَحُقَّتْ", "translit": "ْtَّqُḥَw", "root": "حقق"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 6, "text": "يَٰٓأَيُّهَا ٱلْإِنسَٰنُ إِنَّكَ كَادِحٌ إِلَىٰ رَبِّكَ كَدْحًا فَمُلَٰقِيهِ ", "translation": "O mankind, indeed you are laboring toward your Lord with [great] exertion[1] and will meet it.[2]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "يَٰٓأَيُّهَا", "translit": "āَhُّyَaʾَٰٓy", "root": "ايي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلْإِنسَٰنُ", "translit": "ُnَٰsnِiʾْlٱ", "root": "انس"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "إِنَّكَ", "translit": "َkَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "كَادِحٌ", "translit": "ٌḥِdāَk", "root": "كدح"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "إِلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "رَبِّكَ", "translit": "َkِّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "كَدْحًا", "translit": "āًḥْdَk", "root": "كدح"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "فَمُلَٰقِيهِ", "translit": "ِhyِqَٰlُmَf", "root": "لقي"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 7, "text": "فَأَمَّا مَنْ أُوتِىَ كِتَٰبَهُۥ بِيَمِينِهِۦ ", "translation": "Then as for he who is given his record in his right hand,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَأَمَّا", "translit": "āَّmَaʾَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مَنْ", "translit": "ْnَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أُوتِىَ", "translit": "َàِtwُaʾ", "root": "اتي"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "كِتَٰبَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَbَٰtِk", "root": "كتب"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "بِيَمِينِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِnyِmَyِb", "root": "يمن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 8, "text": "فَسَوْفَ يُحَاسَبُ حِسَابًا يَسِيرًا ", "translation": "He will be judged with an easy account", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَسَوْفَ", "translit": "َfْwَsَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يُحَاسَبُ", "translit": "ُbَsāَḥُy", "root": "حسب"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "حِسَابًا", "translit": "āًbāَsِḥ", "root": "حسب"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "يَسِيرًا", "translit": "āًryِsَy", "root": "يسر"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 9, "text": "وَيَنقَلِبُ إِلَىٰٓ أَهْلِهِۦ مَسْرُورًا ", "translation": "And return to his people in happiness.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَيَنقَلِبُ", "translit": "ُbِlَqnَyَw", "root": "قلب"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "إِلَىٰٓ", "translit": "ٰٓàَlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أَهْلِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِlْhَaʾ", "root": "اهل"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "مَسْرُورًا", "translit": "āًrwُrْsَm", "root": "سرر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 10, "text": "وَأَمَّا مَنْ أُوتِىَ كِتَٰبَهُۥ وَرَآءَ ظَهْرِهِۦ ", "translation": "But as for he who is given his record behind his back,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَأَمَّا", "translit": "āَّmَaʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "مَنْ", "translit": "ْnَm", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أُوتِىَ", "translit": "َàِtwُaʾ", "root": "اتي"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "كِتَٰبَهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَbَٰtِk", "root": "كتب"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "وَرَآءَ", "translit": "َءٓāَrَw", "root": "وري"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "ظَهْرِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِrْhَẓ", "root": "ظهر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 11, "text": "فَسَوْفَ يَدْعُوا۟ ثُبُورًا ", "translation": "He will cry out for destruction", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَسَوْفَ", "translit": "َfْwَsَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَدْعُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُʿعْdَy", "root": "دعو"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ثُبُورًا", "translit": "āًrwُbُht", "root": "ثبر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 12, "text": "وَيَصْلَىٰ سَعِيرًا ", "translation": "And [enter to] burn in a Blaze.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَيَصْلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlْṣَyَw", "root": "صلي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "سَعِيرًا", "translit": "āًryِʿعَs", "root": "سعر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 13, "text": "إِنَّهُۥ كَانَ فِىٓ أَهْلِهِۦ مَسْرُورًا ", "translation": "Indeed, he had [once] been among his people in happiness;", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنَّهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "كَانَ", "translit": "َnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "فِىٓ", "translit": "ٓàِf", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "أَهْلِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِlْhَaʾ", "root": "اهل"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "مَسْرُورًا", "translit": "āًrwُrْsَm", "root": "سرر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 14, "text": "إِنَّهُۥ ظَنَّ أَن لَّن يَحُورَ ", "translation": "Indeed, he had thought he would never return [to Allāh].", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِنَّهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ظَنَّ", "translit": "َّnَẓ", "root": "ظنن"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أَن", "translit": "nَaʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "لَّن", "translit": "nَّl", "root": ""}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "يَحُورَ", "translit": "َrwُḥَy", "root": "حور"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 15, "text": "بَلَىٰٓ إِنَّ رَبَّهُۥ كَانَ بِهِۦ بَصِيرًا ", "translation": "But yes! Indeed, his Lord was ever, of him, Seeing.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "بَلَىٰٓ", "translit": "ٰٓàَlَb", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "إِنَّ", "translit": "َّnِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "رَبَّهُۥ", "translit": "ۥُhَّbَr", "root": "ربب"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "كَانَ", "translit": "َnāَk", "root": "كون"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "بِهِۦ", "translit": "ۦِhِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "بَصِيرًا", "translit": "āًryِṣَb", "root": "بصر"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 16, "text": "فَلَآ أُقْسِمُ بِٱلشَّفَقِ ", "translation": "So I swear by the twilight glow", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَلَآ", "translit": "ٓāَlَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أُقْسِمُ", "translit": "ُmِsْqُaʾ", "root": "قسم"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "بِٱلشَّفَقِ", "translit": "ِqَfَّhslٱِb", "root": "شفق"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 17, "text": "وَٱلَّيْلِ وَمَا وَسَقَ ", "translation": "And [by] the night and what it envelops", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَٱلَّيْلِ", "translit": "ِlْyَّlٱَw", "root": "ليل"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "وَمَا", "translit": "āَmَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "وَسَقَ", "translit": "َqَsَw", "root": "وسق"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 18, "text": "وَٱلْقَمَرِ إِذَا ٱتَّسَقَ ", "translation": "And [by] the moon when it becomes full", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَٱلْقَمَرِ", "translit": "ِrَmَqْlٱَw", "root": "قمر"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "إِذَا", "translit": "āَhdِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ٱتَّسَقَ", "translit": "َqَsَّtٱ", "root": "وسق"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 19, "text": "لَتَرْكَبُنَّ طَبَقًا عَن طَبَقٍ ", "translation": "[That] you will surely embark upon [i.e., experience] state after state.[1]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "لَتَرْكَبُنَّ", "translit": "َّnُbَkْrَtَl", "root": "ركب"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "طَبَقًا", "translit": "āًqَbَṭ", "root": "طبق"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَن", "translit": "nَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "طَبَقٍ", "translit": "ٍqَbَṭ", "root": "طبق"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 20, "text": "فَمَا لَهُمْ لَا يُؤْمِنُونَ ", "translation": "So what is [the matter] with them [that] they do not believe,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَمَا", "translit": "āَmَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "يُؤْمِنُونَ", "translit": "َnwُnِmْwʾُy", "root": "امن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 21, "text": "وَإِذَا قُرِئَ عَلَيْهِمُ ٱلْقُرْءَانُ لَا يَسْجُدُونَ۩ ", "translation": "And when the Qur’ān is recited to them, they do not prostrate [to Allāh]?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَإِذَا", "translit": "āَhdِiʾَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "قُرِئَ", "translit": "َyʾِrُq", "root": "قرا"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَلَيْهِمُ", "translit": "ُmِhْyَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْقُرْءَانُ", "translit": "ُnāَءْrُqْlٱ", "root": "قرا"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "لَا", "translit": "āَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "يَسْجُدُونَ", "translit": "َnwُdُjgْsَy", "root": "سجد"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 22, "text": "بَلِ ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا۟ يُكَذِّبُونَ ", "translation": "But those who have disbelieved deny,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "بَلِ", "translit": "ِlَb", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "كَفَرُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُrَfَk", "root": "كفر"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "يُكَذِّبُونَ", "translit": "َnwُbِّhdَkُy", "root": "كذب"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 23, "text": "وَٱللَّهُ أَعْلَمُ بِمَا يُوعُونَ ", "translation": "And Allāh is most knowing of what they keep within themselves.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَٱللَّهُ", "translit": "ُhَّllٱَw", "root": "اله"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "أَعْلَمُ", "translit": "ُmَlْʿعَaʾ", "root": "علم"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "بِمَا", "translit": "āَmِb", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "يُوعُونَ", "translit": "َnwُʿعwُy", "root": "وعي"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 24, "text": "فَبَشِّرْهُم بِعَذَابٍ أَلِيمٍ ", "translation": "So give them tidings of a painful punishment,", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَبَشِّرْهُم", "translit": "mُhْrِّhsَbَf", "root": "بشر"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "بِعَذَابٍ", "translit": "ٍbāَhdَʿعِb", "root": "عذب"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "أَلِيمٍ", "translit": "ٍmyِlَaʾ", "root": "الم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 25, "text": "إِلَّا ٱلَّذِينَ ءَامَنُوا۟ وَعَمِلُوا۟ ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ لَهُمْ أَجْرٌ غَيْرُ مَمْنُونٍۭ ", "translation": "Except for those who believe and do righteous deeds. For them is a reward uninterrupted.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "إِلَّا", "translit": "āَّlِiʾ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "ءَامَنُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُnَmāَء", "root": "امن"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "وَعَمِلُوا۟", "translit": "۟āwُlِmَʿعَw", "root": "عمل"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلصَّٰلِحَٰتِ", "translit": "ِtَٰḥِlَّٰṣlٱ", "root": "صلح"}, {"id": 6, "arabic": "لَهُمْ", "translit": "ْmُhَl", "root": ""}, {"id": 7, "arabic": "أَجْرٌ", "translit": "ٌrْjgَaʾ", "root": "اجر"}, {"id": 8, "arabic": "غَيْرُ", "translit": "ُrْyَغ", "root": "غير"}, {"id": 9, "arabic": "مَمْنُونٍۭ", "translit": "ٍۭnwُnْmَm", "root": "منن"}], "hasIhya": false}], "tafsir": {"4": [{"arabic": "فارقت الروح الجسد فقد حملت الأرض فمدت حتى ألقت ما فيها وتخلت ولست أطول بجميع موازنة الأحوال والأهوال ولكني أقول بمجرد الموت تقوم عليك هذه القيامة الصغرى ولا يفوتك من القيامة الكبرى شيء مما يخصك بل ما يخص غيرك فإن بقاء الكواكب في حق غيرك ماذا ينفعك وقد انتثرت حواسك التي بها تنتفع بالنظر إلى الكواكب والأعمى يستوى عنده الليل والنهار وكسوف الشمس وانجلاؤها لأنها قد كسفت في حقه دفعة واحدة وهو حصته منها فالانجلاء بعد ذلك حصة غيره ومن انشق رأسه فقد انشقت سماؤه إذ السماء عبارة عما يلي جهة الرأس فمن لا رأس له لا س", "english": "As for the noble ones (al-kirām), it is because of the servant's benefit from their nobility, and because all the angels are noble and righteous (kirām bararah). As for the two writers (al-kātibān), it is for the recording of the good deeds and the evil deeds. They write only upon scrolls folded within the secret of the heart (sirr al-qalb) and folded away from the secret of the heart, so that no one may behold them in this world. For verily, they, their writings, their script, their pages, and the totality of what pertains to them belong to the unseen world and the dominion of sovereignty (ʿālam al-ghayb wa al-malakūt), not to the world of sensory witness (ʿālam al-shahādah). And everything belonging to the world of sovereignty (al-malakūt) is imperceptible to corporeal eyes in this world. Then these scrolls, folded away from him, are unfolded twice: once at the minor resurrection (al-qiyāmah al-ṣughrā) and once at the major resurrection (al-qiyāmah al-kubrā). By the minor resurrection I mean the state of death, for the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said: \"Whoever has died, his resurrection has indeed come to pass\" {«من مات فقد قامت قيامته»}. In this resurrection, the servant is alone, and at that time it is said: {«وَلَقَدْ جِئْتُمُونَا فُرَادَىٰ كَمَا خَلَقْنَاكُمْ أَوَّلَ مَرَّةٍ»} (\"And indeed you have come to Us alone, just as We created you the first time\") — and in it, it is said: {«كَفَىٰ بِنَفْسِكَ الْيَوْمَ عَلَيْكَ حَسِيبًا»} (\"Sufficient is your own soul this day as a reckoner against you\"). As for the major resurrection, which gathers all of creation, he is not alone therein; rather, he may be reckoned before a multitude of creatures, and in it the God-fearing are driven to Paradise and the criminals to the Fire in groups (zumar), not as individuals. The first great terror is the terror of the minor resurrection, and for all the terrors of the major resurrection there is a counterpart in the minor resurrection — such as the earthquake of the earth, for example. For your own particular earth quakes at death, since you know that when an earthquake descends upon a town, it is truly said that \"their earth has quaked,\" even if the surrounding lands have not quaked. Nay, even if only a man's dwelling quakes, the earthquake has occurred relative to him, because he is harmed by the quaking of the entire earth only through the quaking of his own dwelling, not through the quaking of another's dwelling. Thus his share of the earthquake has been fully realized without any diminution. Know that you are an earth created from dust, and your particular share of the dust is only your body. As for the body of another, it is not your share. The earth upon which you sit, in relation to your body, is but a vessel and a place. You fear its quaking only because your body might quake on account of it; otherwise, the air is perpetually in motion and you do not dread it, since your body does not quake because of it. So your share of the earthquake of the entire earth is only the quaking of your body — it is your earth and your particular dust. Your bones are the mountains of your earth; your head is the sky of your earth; your heart is the sun of your earth; your hearing, your sight, and the rest of your faculties are the stars of your sky; the outpouring of sweat from your body is the sea of your earth; your hair is the vegetation of your earth; your limbs are the trees of your earth; and so on to all of your parts. When the pillars of your body collapse through death, then the earth has quaked with its quaking {«إِذَا زُلْزِلَتِ الْأَرْضُ زِلْزَالَهَا»}. When the bones separate from the flesh, then the earth has borne its burdens and the mountains have been crushed to powder {«وَحُمِلَتِ الْأَرْضُ وَالْجِبَالُ فَدُكَّتَا دَكَّةً وَاحِدَةً»}. When the bones crumble, then the mountains have been blown away as dust {«وَنُسِفَتِ الْجِبَالُ نَسْفًا»}. When your heart darkens at death, then the sun has been folded up {«كُوِّرَتِ الشَّمْسُ تَكْوِيرًا»}. When your hearing, sight, and all your senses cease, then the stars have been scattered {«وَانْكَدَرَتِ النُّجُومُ انْكِدَارًا»}. When your brain splits, then the sky has been split asunder {«انْشَقَّتِ السَّمَاءُ انْشِقَاقًا»}. When the sweat of your brow bursts forth from the terror of death, then the seas have been caused to burst forth {«فُجِّرَتِ الْبِحَارُ تَفْجِيرًا»}. When one of your legs entwines with the other — and they are your two mounts — then the pregnant she-camels have been neglected {«عُطِّلَتِ الْعِشَارُ تَعْطِيلًا»}. When the soul departs from the body, then the earth has been lifted and stretched until it casts out what is within it and empties itself {«وَأَلْقَتْ مَا فِيهَا وَتَخَلَّتْ»}. I shall not prolong the enumeration of all the corresponding states and terrors, but I say: by mere death, this minor resurrection comes to pass over you, and nothing of the major resurrection that pertains specifically to you escapes you — rather, only what pertains to another escapes you. For what benefit is the survival of the stars to another, when your senses — through which you benefited by gazing at the stars — have been scattered? The blind man finds night and day equal, and the eclipse of the sun and its clearing likewise, for the sun has been eclipsed for him all at once — that being his share of it — while its clearing thereafter is the share of another. And he whose head has been split open has had his sky split, for the sky is but an expression for what lies in the direction of the head; so whoever has no head has no sky — whence, then, would the survival of the sky for another benefit him? This, then, is the minor resurrection; and the fear after it is greater, and the terror after it is deferred — that is when the Great Calamity arrives {«الطَّامَّةُ الْكُبْرَىٰ»}, particularity is lifted, the heavens and the earth are abolished, the mountains are blown away, and the terrors multiply.", "book_title": "Patience and Gratitude", "section_title_ar": "Section 957", "section_title_en": "The Minor Resurrection: The Microcosmic Earthquake of Death", "section_index": 957, "anchors": "- Root: كرم (karuma)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core root meaning of nobility, generosity, and honor; al-kirām are those distinguished by noble character and beneficence.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Theological nuance: karāmah denotes the honor bestowed by Allah upon His angels and righteous servants, entailing both dignity and generous bestowal.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (Haqiqah): noble, generous in character; Metaphorical (Majaz): the angels described as kirām because of their exalted station and pure obedience, not corporeal nobility.\n- Root: كتب (kataba)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: To write, inscribe, decree; kitāb as a written record; kataba as the act of fixing something in a permanent form.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Theological nuance: al-kātibūn are the recording angels (ḥafaẓah) who inscribe deeds; writing here signifies divine preservation of acts in a register accessible to Allah alone.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: physical inscription on sheets; Metaphorical: the \"writing\" upon the heart's secret core is an immaterial imprinting (naqsh rūḥānī) imperceptible to corporeal sight.\n- Root: موت (mawta)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Death as cessation of animal life; the separation of the soul from the body.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Theological nuance: al-mawt is not annihilation but a transition (intiqlāl) from one abode to another; the minor resurrection (al-qiyāmah al-ṣughrā) is the individual's death, as per the prophetic saying.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: biological death; Metaphorical: \"whoever dies, his resurrection has come to pass\" — the term qiyāmah is transferred (majāz) to the moment of death because the full unveiling of one's deeds begins then.\n- Root: زلزل (zalzala)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Violent shaking, earthquake; intense agitation of the earth.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Theological nuance: the earthquake is a cosmic sign of divine power; in the microcosm, the death-throes of the body are the individual's own \"earthquake.\"\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: seismic tremor of the earth; Metaphorical: the dissolution of one's own body is a true earthquake relative to that person, since only his own frame is his \"earth\" — the rest of the globe is another's concern.\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب التشبيه والتمثيل (Analogy and Proportional Correspondence) — The syntactic structure equates parts of the human microcosm with the macrocosmic phenomena of the Hour, using fa- (consequence) clauses to map each bodily dissolution to its corresponding cosmic portent.", "content_type": "afterlife", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on the journey of the soul, death, and the Hereafter, from 'Patience and Gratitude'", "badge": "Afterlife"}], "6": [{"arabic": "لهواه مودع لعمره سائر إلى مولاه كما قال عز وجل {يا أيها الإنسان إنك كادح إلى ربك كدحا فملاقيه} وقال تعالى {واتقوا الله ويعلمكم الله} وقال تعالى {واتقوا الله واعلموا أنكم ملاقوه} وقال صلى الله عليه وسلم من لم تنهه صلاته عن الفحشاء والمنكر لم يزدد من الله إلا بعدا (5) والصلاة مناجاة فكيف تكون مع الغفلة وقال بكر بن عبد الله يا ابن آدم إذاشئت أن تدخل على مولاك بغير إذن وتكلمه بلا ترجمان دخلت قيل وكيف ذلك قال تسبغ وضوءك وتدخل محرابك فإذا أنت قد دخلت على مولاك بغير إذن فتكلمه بغير ترجمان وعن عائشة رضي الله عنها قالت كان رسول الله صلى ا", "english": "God—Exalted is He—said: {«And establish prayer for My remembrance»} (Q 20:14). And He—Exalted is He—said: {«And be not among the heedless»} (Q 7:205). And He—Mighty and Majestic—said: {«Do not approach prayer while you are intoxicated until you know what you are saying»} (Q 4:43). It was said: \"intoxicated\" from the excess of worldly concern (al-hamm), and it was said: from love of this world.", "book_title": "Mysteries of Prayer", "section_title_ar": "Section 124", "section_title_en": "The Virtue of Humble Devotion (Khusḥūʿ) in Prayer", "section_index": 124, "anchors": "- Root: خشع (Khashaʿa)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: \"الخشوع: التواضع والسكون، وخشع بصره: غضه وأطرقه، وخشعت الأصوات: سكنت وخفضت\"\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الخشوع: الضراعة والاستكانة، وأصله الانخفاض والتطامن، ويقال للصوت الخفيض والطرف المنكسر\"\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): \"Literal: خشع الرجل: خفض رأسه وتواضع. Metaphorical: خشع القلب: خضع وذل وسكن لله\"\n- Root: سكر (Sukr)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: \"السكر: نقيض الصحو، والسكران: الذي غطى عقله، وكل شيء غطى فقد سكر\"\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"السكر: حالة تعرض بين العقل وبين إدراكه، ويستعار لما يغطي العقل من الهم وحب الدنيا\"\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): \"Literal: سكر من الشراب. Metaphorical: سكر الهم وحب الدنيا — ما يغطي العقل عن إدراك المقام\"\n- Root: ندم (Nadama)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: \"الندم: التحسر على ما فات، والندامة: التوبة، والنادم: المتحسر\"\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الندم: انكسار النفس لما فرط، وهو من لوازم التوبة\"\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): \"Literal: ندم على الشيء: تحسر. Metaphorical: تنادم في الصلاة: استحضار التقصير والانكسار بين يدي الله\"\n- Root: وجب (Wajaba)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: \"وجب القلب: اضطرب وخفق، ووجب الشيء: ثبت ولزم، والوجيب: صوت خفقان القلب\"\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"الوجيب: اضطراب القلب من هيبة الأمر وعظمته\"\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): \"Literal: وجب الباب: أغلقه. Metaphorical: وجيب القلب: خفقانه من الخوف والهيبة\"\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الحصر والتقييد بإنما (Restriction & Focused Predication) — \"إنما الصلاة تمسكن\" restricts prayer's essence to humility, excluding distraction and heedlessness.", "content_type": "dua", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on supplications, prayers, and their spiritual power, from 'Mysteries of Prayer'", "badge": "Du'a"}]}, "wordTiming": {"mins